WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.186
Express makes request data easy to reach
through req.body, req.query,

2
00:00:07.266 --> 00:00:11.055
req.params, req.headers, and cookies.

3
00:00:11.135 --> 00:00:13.586
Convenience is not trust.

4
00:00:13.666 --> 00:00:20.910
Every value from the request should be
treated as untrusted until validated.

5
00:00:20.990 --> 00:00:27.230
Body fields, query strings, route
parameters, headers, cookies,

6
00:00:27.310 --> 00:00:34.219
and upload metadata can all influence
database queries, business rules,

7
00:00:34.299 --> 00:00:41.654
redirects, file paths, template rendering,
outbound calls, or side effects.

8
00:00:41.734 --> 00:00:49.423
Validation belongs at the API boundary
before the application relies on the data.

9
00:00:49.503 --> 00:00:55.632
Schema validation helps make expected
request shapes explicit.

10
00:00:55.712 --> 00:01:02.175
A handler should know which fields are
required, which are optional,

11
00:01:02.255 --> 00:01:08.272
what types are allowed, what lengths and
ranges are acceptable,

12
00:01:08.352 --> 00:01:15.818
which enum values are valid, and whether
unexpected fields should be rejected.

13
00:01:15.898 --> 00:01:24.033
For update routes, explicit allowlists
reduce mass assignment risk by choosing which

14
00:01:24.113 --> 00:01:30.911
fields may change instead of accepting
every property the client sends.

15
00:01:30.991 --> 00:01:36.674
Type validation and business-rule
validation are related,

16
00:01:36.754 --> 00:01:40.877
but they are not the same; both may be
needed.

17
00:01:40.957 --> 00:01:48.757
File handling needs particular care
because uploaded content often moves through

18
00:01:48.837 --> 00:01:55.524
storage, scanning, previews, downloads,
and downstream processors.

19
00:01:55.604 --> 00:02:02.958
A secure design considers size limits,
type expectations, storage location,

20
00:02:03.038 --> 00:02:11.396
access control, temporary file cleanup,
and scanning requirements where appropriate.

21
00:02:11.476 --> 00:02:18.273
Avoid using unvalidated input in
filesystem paths, command execution,

22
00:02:18.353 --> 00:02:25.708
database queries, redirects, template
rendering, or service destinations.

23
00:02:25.788 --> 00:02:33.700
The defensive pattern is predictable
parsing followed by narrow, intentional use.
